;;; A rule with a parameter whose `:match` is `()` never fires — M1f **W31**,
;;; register row `W31/empty-match-activator` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`),
;;; banked by S1f.5.0 (2026-11-08) from S1f.5.9's case (P1f.5's F12), filed
;;; `open` and owned by S1f.5.9, on the user's ruling of 2026-11-07 on F12.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A rule `r` with one parameter and no premise, concluding `(hit ?x)`, and
;;; its activator `(r a)`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; An empty conjunction is true, so the rule fires once per activator fact,
;;; with only its parameters bound (F12's ruling): root holds `(hit a :rule
;;; r)`, and R's minimal line is root's state.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answers ────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The rule loads and never fires (`ein saturate FILE --dump`): root holds no
;;; `hit`, `(hit a)` is a candidate, and R is four states, exit 0 (`ein solve
;;; FILE` and `ein oracle FILE` at `ec004a48`, the engine `916d97ac`'s,
;;; release and debug alike).
;;;
;;; ── Since M1f S1f.5.9 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `:match ()` is the empty conjunction since T1f.5.9.2 (2026-11-09), so `r`
;;; fires once on its activator: root holds `(hit a :rule r)`, H is `(p a)`,
;;; and R two states, the answer above by hand. The register's `now` is that
;;; answer; the section above is the record of the one it replaced.

(relation q Node) (relation p Node) (relation hit Node)
(q a)
(rule r (?x) :match () :assert (hit ?x))
(r a)
